    "abstract": "U-Net is a network and training strategy that relies on strong data augmentation to use few annotated samples efficiently. A contracting path captures context and a symmetric expanding path enables precise localization. Trained end-to-end from very few images, it outperforms the prior best method on the ISBI EM segmentation challenge and wins the ISBI 2015 cell tracking challenge by a large margin.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "A U-shaped network with crop-and-concatenate skip connections enables precise localization from few training images.",
      "Elastic deformations are key to learning invariances from very few annotated images.",
      "A weighted loss with w0=10, sigma≈5 forces the network to learn separation borders between touching cells.",
      "Overlap-tile strategy with mirror padding allows seamless segmentation of arbitrarily large images.",
      "EM segmentation challenge warping error 0.000353; PhC-U373 IoU 0.9203; DIC-HeLa IoU 0.7756."
    ],
